module gunbc.replacement_cut


data replacement_cut_model_note: String = "THE MECHANICAL PLANNING CARRIER FOR REPLACEMENT MIGRATIONS (DESIGN section 3 standing rule, operator-directed 2026-08-15; hardened per the 2026-08-15 planning-thread review). A ReplacementCut names one consumer-relative boundary: the exact old root consumer, subject population and semantic contract; the Y authority proposed at that boundary; the X region deleted at cutover; the boundary-consumer census with every consumer's earned disposition; X's permitted external roles from a CLOSED vocabulary (a forbidden role -- fallback, internal resolver, production second opinion -- has no constructor); and the evidence dispositions. Construction encodes the greedy root-first search: why_not_higher is a required field, so a cut cannot be authored without stating either that its boundary is outermost or which parent cut's refusal pushed it down -- the descended arm names the parent by ReplacementCutId, a joinable typed reference, never prose alone. A THIRD ARM, DescentParentUnauthored, carries the state a real first subject actually lands in: this boundary is not outermost AND no cut has been authored at the boundary above it, so there is no id to name. It names the intended parent BOUNDARY and a basis, deliberately carrying no identifier -- an optional id would be the same joinable-but-unresolvable hazard wearing a Maybe. Without it the honest state has no constructor and the carrier forces a false one, both falses being worse than they look: OutermostBoundary mints a sealed, digest-bound, sole_constructor AdmittedReplacementCutPlan asserting a boundary is outermost when it is not, and a minted parent id is false AND JOINS CLEANLY, which no reader can detect. See replacement_cut_unjoined_parent_rung_note for what this arm does NOT fix.\n\nADMISSION IS PLAN ADMISSION, and the vocabulary says so: admit_replacement_cut_plan judges the AUTHORED PLAN's completeness and internal coherence, not the world. It refuses, all causes counted, on: any undecided consumer or evidence row; any surviving consumer without a named coverage authority; coverage or replacement naming the old root itself (fallback wearing a disposition); an empty covered region; old and new root identical; a census enumerated yet empty (the bottom-as-answer conflation -- a genuinely consumer-free boundary is declared with BoundaryDeclaredEmpty and a basis, never left as an ambiguous empty list); an ExternalXRoles list enumerated yet empty (the same conflation on the oracle axis -- no-oracle-needed is the justified NoExternalOracleRequired arm, never an empty list); a self-referential descent; and any duplicated consumer, evidence subject, or region member (one subject, one disposition -- a duplicate is a fork whether or not the copies agree). The verdict is SEALED AND BOUND twice over: AdmittedReplacementCutPlan is a sole_constructor record only this module can build -- a cross-module construction or cast refuses at compile time (04_infer sole_constructor_construction_diags) -- and its one in-module mint, mint_admitted, is admit_callers-sealed to admit_replacement_cut_plan alone, so no importer can reach a verdict except through the checks. The digest binds the verdict to the exact plan it judged: an edited plan stops matching, and admitted_matches_plan is the recompute check.\n\nWHAT PLAN ADMISSION DOES NOT ESTABLISH, stated per DESIGN 4b rung honesty: the authored census is not proven equal to the real boundary population -- an omitted consumer cannot be detected at this grain, because no independently produced consumer/obligation/evidence/region observation exists yet to join against; coverage authorities are named, not proven to cover; OutermostBoundary is an authored claim pending a boundary-census receipt; a descended cut's parent refusal is a typed reference pending executed refusal receipts; retirement names its reason pending a retirement-receipt authority. Those two-way exact identity joins, the attempt layer (backedge, parity, refusal preservation, executed deletion), derived cut standing, the outcome ledger, and the roadmap projection are the migration-cut authority program -- the named next layer, deliberately not pre-built as string-shaped promises. NO ROADMAP NODE IS STRUCTURALLY REGISTERED TO A CUT YET: RoadmapNode carries no cut field, and the typed projection in which a lane's contract, shadow, parity and cutover-plus-deletion nodes derive from ONE admitted plan -- cutover and deletion one accepted state, a deeper cut addable only under an exact parent refusal, unregistered migration work red -- is a future obligation of that program, not a present fact."

data replacement_cut_unjoined_parent_rung_note: String = "RUNG HONESTY (DESIGN 4b), declared rather than left to be rediscovered: DescendedFromRefusedCut.parent_cut IS AN UNJOINED REFERENCE. ReplacementCutId is a brand over NonEmptyStr, so every string inhabits it, and the only check applied to why_not_higher anywhere in this module is SelfReferentialDescent -- parent equals this cut's own identity. A plan naming a parent cut that exists nowhere in any tree is ADMITTED, sealed and digest-bound like any other. MEASURED, not read: probe_admits_nonexistent_parent returned true against a parent id of cut-that-exists-nowhere-in-any-tree-zzz, with probe_control_refuses_undecided returning false in the same run as the positive control proving admission is not vacuous (gentle-dove-833, 2026-08-16, base 7f5fa6a94ec1). Those three probes are enrolled in replacement_cut_witness_test as permanent regression controls.\n\nRUNG: mitigatable. CEILING AND WHY IT IS NOT REACHED TODAY: an existence check needs a registry of authored cuts to join against, and THIS CARRIER HAS ZERO PRODUCTION ROWS -- every ReplacementCut value in the tree is a synthetic fixture in its own witness, so there is nothing for a check to consult. The gap is therefore not buildable now, and adding the third arm does not close it: DescentParentUnauthored makes the honest state WRITABLE, it does not make the dishonest one unwritable. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a cut registry carrying real authored rows, at which point parent_cut becomes an identity join and unjoined_parent_admits_declared_gap goes red -- which is the signal to close this note, not a failure.\n\nWHY THE GAP SURVIVED A 423-LINE EXECUTING WITNESS SUITE: every input those witnesses exercise was invented by the same author as the type, so the state a real subject lands in was never reachable from them. A synthetic witness tests the refusals its author thought of; a first production row tests the ones nobody did. This carrier's first real subject -- the interpreter cut, descended from an engine cut nobody has authored -- hit the hole on the first field it filled."

type ReplacementCutId = std.types.NonEmptyStr where brand("ReplacementCutId")

type CoverageClaim
  = Covered { by: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | CoverageOpen

type ConsumerDisposition
  = RetainSameContract { justification: std.types.NonEmptyStr, coverage: CoverageClaim }
  | RetainChangedContract { terminal_contract: std.types.NonEmptyStr, justification: std.types.NonEmptyStr, coverage: CoverageClaim }
  | ReplacedByY { new_authority: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | EvidenceOnly { surviving_claim: std.types.NonEmptyStr, reenrolled_witness: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | Retire { reason: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | Undecided

type BoundaryConsumer { consumer: std.types.NonEmptyStr, disposition: ConsumerDisposition }

type BoundaryCensus
  = ConsumersEnumerated { consumers: std.types.List<BoundaryConsumer> }
  | BoundaryDeclaredEmpty { basis: std.types.NonEmptyStr }

type HigherBoundaryAnswer
  = OutermostBoundary
  | DescendedFromRefusedCut { parent_cut: ReplacementCutId, refusal_summary: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | DescentParentUnauthored { intended_parent_boundary: std.types.NonEmptyStr, basis: std.types.NonEmptyStr }

type EvidenceDisposition
  = ReenrollAgainstY { evidence: std.types.NonEmptyStr, surviving_claim: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | ReplaceEvidence { old_evidence: std.types.NonEmptyStr, new_evidence: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | RetireEvidence { evidence: std.types.NonEmptyStr, retired_subject: std.types.NonEmptyStr, retirement_reason: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | EvidenceUndecided { evidence: std.types.NonEmptyStr }

type ExternalXRole
  = BootstrapProducer
  | ExternalDifferentialOracle
  | MechanicalCorpusRewriter
  | HistoricalMeasurementSource

type ExternalXAnswer
  = ExternalXRoles { roles: std.types.List<ExternalXRole> }
  | NoExternalOracleRequired { justification: std.types.NonEmptyStr }

type ReplacementCut {
  identity: ReplacementCutId
  old_root_consumer: std.types.NonEmptyStr
  subject: std.types.NonEmptyStr
  contract: std.types.NonEmptyStr
  new_root: std.types.NonEmptyStr
  why_not_higher: HigherBoundaryAnswer
  covered_region: List<std.types.NonEmptyStr>
  boundary_census: BoundaryCensus
  external_x: ExternalXAnswer
  evidence_dispositions: List<EvidenceDisposition>
}

type CutRefusalCause
  = UndispositionedConsumer { consumer: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | UncoveredSurvivingConsumer { consumer: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | UndispositionedEvidence { evidence: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | CoveredByOldRoot { consumer: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | ReplacementNamesOldRoot { consumer: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | ConsumerDuplicated { consumer: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | EvidenceDuplicated { evidence: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | RegionMemberDuplicated { member: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | EnumeratedCensusEmpty
  | ExternalRolesEnumeratedEmpty
  | EmptyCoveredRegion
  | NewRootEqualsOldRoot
  | SelfReferentialDescent

type AdmittedReplacementCutPlan sole_constructor {
  cut_identity: ReplacementCutId
  criteria_digest: std.content_hash.Fnv1a64Structural
  retained_count: Int
  replaced_count: Int
  evidence_only_count: Int
  retired_count: Int
  covered_region_count: Int
}

type PlanAdmission
  = PlanAdmitted { admitted: AdmittedReplacementCutPlan }
  | PlanRefused { causes: std.types.List<CutRefusalCause> }

type CountStanding = CountZero | CountPositive

fn count_standing(count: Int) -> CountStanding {
  if count == 0 { CountZero } else { CountPositive }
}

fn nes_eq(a: std.types.NonEmptyStr, b: std.types.NonEmptyStr) -> Bool {
  (a as String) == (b as String)
}

fn nes_seen(xs: List<std.types.NonEmptyStr>, x: std.types.NonEmptyStr) -> Bool {
  fold(xs, init: false, f: fn(acc, item) { acc || nes_eq(a: item, b: x) })
}

fn coverage_causes(
  acc: List<CutRefusalCause>,
  consumer: std.types.NonEmptyStr,
  old_root_consumer: std.types.NonEmptyStr,
  cov: CoverageClaim,
) -> List<CutRefusalCause> {
  match cov {
    CoverageOpen => std.algebra.Cons { head: UncoveredSurvivingConsumer { consumer: consumer }, tail: acc }
    Covered { by: authority } =>
      match nes_eq(a: authority, b: old_root_consumer) {
        true => std.algebra.Cons { head: CoveredByOldRoot { consumer: consumer }, tail: acc }
        false => acc
      }
  }
}

fn consumer_causes(
  acc: List<CutRefusalCause>,
  old_root_consumer: std.types.NonEmptyStr,
  c: BoundaryConsumer,
) -> List<CutRefusalCause> {
  match c.disposition {
    Undecided => std.algebra.Cons { head: UndispositionedConsumer { consumer: c.consumer }, tail: acc }
    RetainSameContract { justification: _, coverage: cov } =>
      coverage_causes(acc: acc, consumer: c.consumer, old_root_consumer: old_root_consumer, cov: cov)
    RetainChangedContract { terminal_contract: _, justification: _, coverage: cov } =>
      coverage_causes(acc: acc, consumer: c.consumer, old_root_consumer: old_root_consumer, cov: cov)
    ReplacedByY { new_authority: authority } =>
      match nes_eq(a: authority, b: old_root_consumer) {
        true => std.algebra.Cons { head: ReplacementNamesOldRoot { consumer: c.consumer }, tail: acc }
        false => acc
      }
    EvidenceOnly { surviving_claim: _, reenrolled_witness: _ } => acc
    Retire { reason: _ } => acc
  }
}

fn evidence_causes(acc: List<CutRefusalCause>, e: EvidenceDisposition) -> List<CutRefusalCause> {
  match e {
    EvidenceUndecided { evidence: w } => std.algebra.Cons { head: UndispositionedEvidence { evidence: w }, tail: acc }
    ReenrollAgainstY { evidence: _, surviving_claim: _ } => acc
    ReplaceEvidence { old_evidence: _, new_evidence: _ } => acc
    RetireEvidence { evidence: _, retired_subject: _, retirement_reason: _ } => acc
  }
}

fn evidence_key(e: EvidenceDisposition) -> std.types.NonEmptyStr {
  match e {
    ReenrollAgainstY { evidence: w, surviving_claim: _ } => w
    ReplaceEvidence { old_evidence: w, new_evidence: _ } => w
    RetireEvidence { evidence: w, retired_subject: _, retirement_reason: _ } => w
    EvidenceUndecided { evidence: w } => w
  }
}

type ConsumerDupState { seen: std.types.List<std.types.NonEmptyStr>, causes: std.types.List<CutRefusalCause> }

fn consumer_duplicate_causes(
  acc: List<CutRefusalCause>,
  consumers: List<BoundaryConsumer>,
) -> List<CutRefusalCause> {
  let end_state = fold(
    consumers,
    init: ConsumerDupState { seen: [], causes: acc },
    f: fn(state, c) {
      match nes_seen(xs: state.seen, x: c.consumer) {
        true => ConsumerDupState {
          seen: state.seen,
          causes: std.algebra.Cons { head: ConsumerDuplicated { consumer: c.consumer }, tail: state.causes },
        }
        false => ConsumerDupState {
          seen: std.algebra.Cons { head: c.consumer, tail: state.seen },
          causes: state.causes,
        }
      }
    },
  )
  end_state.causes
}

fn evidence_dup_step(state: ConsumerDupState, key: std.types.NonEmptyStr) -> ConsumerDupState {
  match nes_seen(xs: state.seen, x: key) {
    true => ConsumerDupState {
      seen: state.seen,
      causes: std.algebra.Cons { head: EvidenceDuplicated { evidence: key }, tail: state.causes },
    }
    false => ConsumerDupState {
      seen: std.algebra.Cons { head: key, tail: state.seen },
      causes: state.causes,
    }
  }
}

fn evidence_duplicate_causes(
  acc: List<CutRefusalCause>,
  rows: List<EvidenceDisposition>,
) -> List<CutRefusalCause> {
  let end_state = fold(
    rows,
    init: ConsumerDupState { seen: [], causes: acc },
    f: fn(state, e) { evidence_dup_step(state: state, key: evidence_key(e: e)) },
  )
  end_state.causes
}

fn region_causes(acc: List<CutRefusalCause>, region: List<std.types.NonEmptyStr>) -> List<CutRefusalCause> {
  let dup_state = fold(
    region,
    init: ConsumerDupState { seen: [], causes: acc },
    f: fn(state, member) {
      match nes_seen(xs: state.seen, x: member) {
        true => ConsumerDupState {
          seen: state.seen,
          causes: std.algebra.Cons { head: RegionMemberDuplicated { member: member }, tail: state.causes },
        }
        false => ConsumerDupState {
          seen: std.algebra.Cons { head: member, tail: state.seen },
          causes: state.causes,
        }
      }
    },
  )
  match count_standing(count: list_length(items: region)) {
    CountZero => std.algebra.Cons { head: EmptyCoveredRegion, tail: dup_state.causes }
    CountPositive => dup_state.causes
  }
}

fn enumerated_consumer_causes(
  acc: List<CutRefusalCause>,
  old_root_consumer: std.types.NonEmptyStr,
  rows: List<BoundaryConsumer>,
) -> List<CutRefusalCause> {
  let disposition_acc = fold(
    rows,
    init: acc,
    f: fn(inner, c) { consumer_causes(acc: inner, old_root_consumer: old_root_consumer, c: c) },
  )
  consumer_duplicate_causes(acc: disposition_acc, consumers: rows)
}

fn census_causes(
  acc: List<CutRefusalCause>,
  old_root_consumer: std.types.NonEmptyStr,
  census: BoundaryCensus,
) -> List<CutRefusalCause> {
  match census {
    BoundaryDeclaredEmpty { basis: _ } => acc
    ConsumersEnumerated { consumers: rows } =>
      match count_standing(count: list_length(items: rows)) {
        CountZero => std.algebra.Cons { head: EnumeratedCensusEmpty, tail: acc }
        CountPositive => enumerated_consumer_causes(acc: acc, old_root_consumer: old_root_consumer, rows: rows)
      }
  }
}

fn external_x_causes(acc: List<CutRefusalCause>, x: ExternalXAnswer) -> List<CutRefusalCause> {
  match x {
    NoExternalOracleRequired { justification: _ } => acc
    ExternalXRoles { roles: rs } =>
      match count_standing(count: list_length(items: rs)) {
        CountZero => std.algebra.Cons { head: ExternalRolesEnumeratedEmpty, tail: acc }
        CountPositive => acc
      }
  }
}

fn root_identity_causes(acc: List<CutRefusalCause>, cut: ReplacementCut) -> List<CutRefusalCause> {
  let after_root = match nes_eq(a: cut.new_root, b: cut.old_root_consumer) {
    true => std.algebra.Cons { head: NewRootEqualsOldRoot, tail: acc }
    false => acc
  }
  match cut.why_not_higher {
    OutermostBoundary => after_root
    DescendedFromRefusedCut { parent_cut: parent, refusal_summary: _ } =>
      match nes_eq(a: parent as std.types.NonEmptyStr, b: cut.identity as std.types.NonEmptyStr) {
        true => std.algebra.Cons { head: SelfReferentialDescent, tail: after_root }
        false => after_root
      }
    DescentParentUnauthored { intended_parent_boundary: boundary, basis: _ } =>
      match nes_eq(a: boundary, b: cut.old_root_consumer) {
        true => std.algebra.Cons { head: SelfReferentialDescent, tail: after_root }
        false => after_root
      }
  }
}

type DispositionCounts {
  retained: Int
  replaced: Int
  evidence_only: Int
  retired: Int
  undecided: Int
}

fn census_consumers(census: BoundaryCensus) -> List<BoundaryConsumer> {
  match census {
    ConsumersEnumerated { consumers: rows } => rows
    BoundaryDeclaredEmpty { basis: _ } => []
  }
}

fn count_dispositions(consumers: List<BoundaryConsumer>) -> DispositionCounts {
  fold(
    consumers,
    init: DispositionCounts { retained: 0, replaced: 0, evidence_only: 0, retired: 0, undecided: 0 },
    f: fn(acc, c) {
      match c.disposition {
        RetainSameContract { justification: _, coverage: _ } =>
          DispositionCounts { retained: acc.retained + 1, replaced: acc.replaced, evidence_only: acc.evidence_only, retired: acc.retired, undecided: acc.undecided }
        RetainChangedContract { terminal_contract: _, justification: _, coverage: _ } =>
          DispositionCounts { retained: acc.retained + 1, replaced: acc.replaced, evidence_only: acc.evidence_only, retired: acc.retired, undecided: acc.undecided }
        ReplacedByY { new_authority: _ } =>
          DispositionCounts { retained: acc.retained, replaced: acc.replaced + 1, evidence_only: acc.evidence_only, retired: acc.retired, undecided: acc.undecided }
        EvidenceOnly { surviving_claim: _, reenrolled_witness: _ } =>
          DispositionCounts { retained: acc.retained, replaced: acc.replaced, evidence_only: acc.evidence_only + 1, retired: acc.retired, undecided: acc.undecided }
        Retire { reason: _ } =>
          DispositionCounts { retained: acc.retained, replaced: acc.replaced, evidence_only: acc.evidence_only, retired: acc.retired + 1, undecided: acc.undecided }
        Undecided =>
          DispositionCounts { retained: acc.retained, replaced: acc.replaced, evidence_only: acc.evidence_only, retired: acc.retired, undecided: acc.undecided + 1 }
      }
    },
  )
}

fn nes_digest(value: std.types.NonEmptyStr) -> std.content_hash.Fnv1a64Structural {
  content_hash_atom(value: value)
}

fn tag_digest(tag: std.types.NonEmptyStr) -> std.content_hash.Fnv1a64Structural {
  content_hash_atom(value: tag)
}

fn nes_list_digest(tag: std.types.NonEmptyStr, items: List<std.types.NonEmptyStr>) -> std.content_hash.Fnv1a64Structural {
  fold(
    items,
    init: tag_digest(tag: tag),
    f: fn(acc, item) { content_hash_combine_structural(left: acc, right: nes_digest(value: item)) },
  )
}

fn coverage_digest(cov: CoverageClaim) -> std.content_hash.Fnv1a64Structural {
  match cov {
    Covered { by: authority } => content_hash_tagged_structural(tag: "covered" as std.types.NonEmptyStr, payload: nes_digest(value: authority))
    CoverageOpen => tag_digest(tag: "coverage-open" as std.types.NonEmptyStr)
  }
}

fn disposition_digest(d: ConsumerDisposition) -> std.content_hash.Fnv1a64Structural {
  match d {
    RetainSameContract { justification: j, coverage: cov } =>
      content_hash_tagged_structural(
        tag: "retain-same" as std.types.NonEmptyStr,
        payload: content_hash_combine_structural(left: nes_digest(value: j), right: coverage_digest(cov: cov)),
      )
    RetainChangedContract { terminal_contract: t, justification: j, coverage: cov } =>
      content_hash_tagged_structural(
        tag: "retain-changed" as std.types.NonEmptyStr,
        payload: content_hash_combine_structural(
          left: content_hash_combine_structural(left: nes_digest(value: t), right: nes_digest(value: j)),
          right: coverage_digest(cov: cov),
        ),
      )
    ReplacedByY { new_authority: a } =>
      content_hash_tagged_structural(tag: "replaced-by-y" as std.types.NonEmptyStr, payload: nes_digest(value: a))
    EvidenceOnly { surviving_claim: sc, reenrolled_witness: w } =>
      content_hash_tagged_structural(
        tag: "evidence-only" as std.types.NonEmptyStr,
        payload: content_hash_combine_structural(left: nes_digest(value: sc), right: nes_digest(value: w)),
      )
    Retire { reason: r } =>
      content_hash_tagged_structural(tag: "retire" as std.types.NonEmptyStr, payload: nes_digest(value: r))
    Undecided => tag_digest(tag: "undecided" as std.types.NonEmptyStr)
  }
}

fn census_digest(census: BoundaryCensus) -> std.content_hash.Fnv1a64Structural {
  match census {
    BoundaryDeclaredEmpty { basis: b } =>
      content_hash_tagged_structural(tag: "boundary-declared-empty" as std.types.NonEmptyStr, payload: nes_digest(value: b))
    ConsumersEnumerated { consumers: rows } =>
      fold(
        rows,
        init: tag_digest(tag: "consumers-enumerated" as std.types.NonEmptyStr),
        f: fn(acc, c) {
          content_hash_combine_structural(
            left: acc,
            right: content_hash_combine_structural(left: nes_digest(value: c.consumer), right: disposition_digest(d: c.disposition)),
          )
        },
      )
  }
}

fn evidence_row_digest(e: EvidenceDisposition) -> std.content_hash.Fnv1a64Structural {
  match e {
    ReenrollAgainstY { evidence: w, surviving_claim: sc } =>
      content_hash_tagged_structural(
        tag: "reenroll" as std.types.NonEmptyStr,
        payload: content_hash_combine_structural(left: nes_digest(value: w), right: nes_digest(value: sc)),
      )
    ReplaceEvidence { old_evidence: o, new_evidence: n } =>
      content_hash_tagged_structural(
        tag: "replace-evidence" as std.types.NonEmptyStr,
        payload: content_hash_combine_structural(left: nes_digest(value: o), right: nes_digest(value: n)),
      )
    RetireEvidence { evidence: w, retired_subject: s, retirement_reason: r } =>
      content_hash_tagged_structural(
        tag: "retire-evidence" as std.types.NonEmptyStr,
        payload: content_hash_combine_structural(
          left: content_hash_combine_structural(left: nes_digest(value: w), right: nes_digest(value: s)),
          right: nes_digest(value: r),
        ),
      )
    EvidenceUndecided { evidence: w } =>
      content_hash_tagged_structural(tag: "evidence-undecided" as std.types.NonEmptyStr, payload: nes_digest(value: w))
  }
}

fn higher_boundary_digest(h: HigherBoundaryAnswer) -> std.content_hash.Fnv1a64Structural {
  match h {
    OutermostBoundary => tag_digest(tag: "outermost" as std.types.NonEmptyStr)
    DescendedFromRefusedCut { parent_cut: parent, refusal_summary: r } =>
      content_hash_tagged_structural(
        tag: "descended" as std.types.NonEmptyStr,
        payload: content_hash_combine_structural(left: nes_digest(value: parent as std.types.NonEmptyStr), right: nes_digest(value: r)),
      )
    DescentParentUnauthored { intended_parent_boundary: boundary, basis: b } =>
      content_hash_tagged_structural(
        tag: "descent-parent-unauthored" as std.types.NonEmptyStr,
        payload: content_hash_combine_structural(left: nes_digest(value: boundary), right: nes_digest(value: b)),
      )
  }
}

fn external_x_role_digest(r: ExternalXRole) -> std.content_hash.Fnv1a64Structural {
  match r {
    BootstrapProducer => tag_digest(tag: "bootstrap-producer" as std.types.NonEmptyStr)
    ExternalDifferentialOracle => tag_digest(tag: "external-differential-oracle" as std.types.NonEmptyStr)
    MechanicalCorpusRewriter => tag_digest(tag: "mechanical-corpus-rewriter" as std.types.NonEmptyStr)
    HistoricalMeasurementSource => tag_digest(tag: "historical-measurement-source" as std.types.NonEmptyStr)
  }
}

fn external_x_digest(a: ExternalXAnswer) -> std.content_hash.Fnv1a64Structural {
  match a {
    NoExternalOracleRequired { justification: j } =>
      content_hash_tagged_structural(tag: "no-external-oracle" as std.types.NonEmptyStr, payload: nes_digest(value: j))
    ExternalXRoles { roles: rs } =>
      fold(
        rs,
        init: tag_digest(tag: "external-x-roles" as std.types.NonEmptyStr),
        f: fn(acc, r) { content_hash_combine_structural(left: acc, right: external_x_role_digest(r: r)) },
      )
  }
}

fn replacement_cut_plan_digest(cut: ReplacementCut) -> std.content_hash.Fnv1a64Structural {
  let identity_part = content_hash_combine_structural(
    left: nes_digest(value: cut.identity as std.types.NonEmptyStr),
    right: nes_digest(value: cut.old_root_consumer),
  )
  let contract_part = content_hash_combine_structural(
    left: nes_digest(value: cut.subject),
    right: content_hash_combine_structural(left: nes_digest(value: cut.contract), right: nes_digest(value: cut.new_root)),
  )
  let structure_part = content_hash_combine_structural(
    left: higher_boundary_digest(h: cut.why_not_higher),
    right: nes_list_digest(tag: "covered-region" as std.types.NonEmptyStr, items: cut.covered_region),
  )
  let population_part = content_hash_combine_structural(
    left: census_digest(census: cut.boundary_census),
    right: fold(
      cut.evidence_dispositions,
      init: external_x_digest(a: cut.external_x),
      f: fn(acc, e) { content_hash_combine_structural(left: acc, right: evidence_row_digest(e: e)) },
    ),
  )
  content_hash_combine_structural(
    left: content_hash_combine_structural(left: identity_part, right: contract_part),
    right: content_hash_combine_structural(left: structure_part, right: population_part),
  )
}

fn mint_admitted(cut: ReplacementCut, counts: DispositionCounts) -> PlanAdmission
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.replacement_cut", decl_name: "admit_replacement_cut_plan"),
  ]
  = PlanAdmitted {
    admitted: AdmittedReplacementCutPlan {
      cut_identity: cut.identity,
      criteria_digest: replacement_cut_plan_digest(cut: cut),
      retained_count: counts.retained,
      replaced_count: counts.replaced,
      evidence_only_count: counts.evidence_only,
      retired_count: counts.retired,
      covered_region_count: list_length(items: cut.covered_region),
    },
  }

fn admit_replacement_cut_plan(cut: ReplacementCut) -> PlanAdmission {
  let root_acc = root_identity_causes(acc: [], cut: cut)
  let census_acc = census_causes(acc: root_acc, old_root_consumer: cut.old_root_consumer, census: cut.boundary_census)
  let oracle_acc = external_x_causes(acc: census_acc, x: cut.external_x)
  let evidence_disposition_acc = fold(
    cut.evidence_dispositions,
    init: oracle_acc,
    f: fn(acc, e) { evidence_causes(acc: acc, e: e) },
  )
  let evidence_acc = evidence_duplicate_causes(acc: evidence_disposition_acc, rows: cut.evidence_dispositions)
  let all_causes = region_causes(acc: evidence_acc, region: cut.covered_region)
  match count_standing(count: list_length(items: all_causes)) {
    CountZero => mint_admitted(cut: cut, counts: count_dispositions(consumers: census_consumers(census: cut.boundary_census)))
    CountPositive => PlanRefused { causes: all_causes }
  }
}

fn admitted_matches_plan(admitted: AdmittedReplacementCutPlan, cut: ReplacementCut) -> Bool {
  nes_eq(a: admitted.cut_identity as std.types.NonEmptyStr, b: cut.identity as std.types.NonEmptyStr)
    && content_hash_eq_structural(left: admitted.criteria_digest, right: replacement_cut_plan_digest(cut: cut))
}
